Note: I wrote most of this ages ago... I found it on my hardrive and
realized, I hadn't posted this ascension yet? The horror!

My fourth ascension *yays* This game started out kinda unusual... I
wanted to try a game with a wizard after losing like, dozens and
dozens of Rangers, Priests, and various other random classes, but I
was keeping a steady vegan diet, and trying to go weaponless but
bombing horribly. I managed to do s'kay that way :)

I took ages to actually write this, and the actual ascension was a
long while back. After finishing the game like this I felt really put
off by nethack for the longest time. So if I gloss over details a
little please forgive me, but I'll try to make this as yummy as
possible. I mean... it wasn't exactly easy, but this was the first
time an ascension was like "I don't really want to die, why don't I
try something completely crazy?"

Now just a little side mention, after doing several nearly
ascenscions, wishless, nethack is definantly feeling like much less of
a challenge. Something so has to be done about gehommen (although...
being wishless does make it alot more interesting) it really lacks
everything that makes all the above levels fun. You'll never find a
random shopkeeper, a hall of lepricons, a temple, a den on 'trices,
bunches of soldiers, treasure rooms, or anything you havn't seen
before aside from mazes, more mazes, and prefab levels. We have
challenges, which honestly could keep me having fun forever, but
honestly... if Gehommen were kinda like the levels above it, it would
be alot more fun. To make a little comparison, the Gnomish mines have
very much the same design as Gehommen but are never boring. It's
shorter, you bump into it when you're insanely ill prepared, so it
tends to be alot more of a blast. By the time you bump into gehommen
you don't need mazes with tons of shiny new toys to play with, you
need a little bit of challenge and lots of trickery. Okay done with
ranting and on to story.

Going vegan is kinda tricky... you have horribly limited options to
prevent stoning. I only found one potion of acid the whole game, and
eating lizards wasn't an option... (no tinning for some silly reason)
On top of that you like have very little option for intrinsics,
especially if you arn't playing monk. I wasn't going athiest though,
so sacrificing made up for that extremely well.

At the beginning of the dungeons of doom it looked a little eerie, and
I immidiately tossed my quarterstaff aside, I never wanted to use it.
=46rom then on I didn't use a single weilded weapon, aside from the
occasional pick-axe, with no accidents whatsoever.

I went carefully through the first level, thinking I would go athiest
as well... but... a quick little accident just one level into the the
dungeon totally ruined that. My poor little kitten, she stepped into a
rock trap and died a quick practically painless death. I felt kinda
guilty for it in a non-game sense, but there wasn't much I could do. I
played cautiously, throwing Sting and other daggers I picked up along
the way and weilding nothing but my bare hands. It was tricky, slow,
very tedious, but it proved to be good practice.

I picked up a nice magic lamp on the way down, after fending off a
horde of killer bees, a ghoul, several soldier ants, and a few other
nasties with daggers and kittens and force bolts (did I mention this
was a double bones level?) picking up... not much else.

With a little bit of patience, a fresh new kitten, I looted out a
scroll and a book store, identifying identify, and starting off with a
spell book of identify, and hardly anything else. I kept practicing my
"detect monsters" spell... and spicing it up a little with occasional
blasts of force bolt at nasty little monsters. I worked my way into
minetown without going down much deeper, gathering a small horde of
little doggies and kittens on the way. I got through minetown, and had
to fight off the town watch after a little accident involving a
monster of some sort, and a flying dagger.

I had lost my friendly no-god conduct by this point, so cleaned out
the shops and shopkeepers (aside from the general store, and the
friendly lighting shop) and donated a whole bunch as my horde of pets
roamed around picking off monster stragglers, getting a little bit of
protection. What to do from here? I have a horde of kitties... so I
should be fine, and there isn't anything to worry about, I'll just
work down, get the luckstone, and maybe get a few levels on the way?
Well... it didn't turn out that well.

I go around one level below minetown, and suddenly, I step down a trap
door. I fall all the way to the bottom of the mines and get surrounded
quickly by vampires and mummies. As I fend off the horde with my
daggers and force bolts I'm quickly overwelmed, and make a hasty
retreat up the stairs. This is getting nasty.....

One level up I fight off the usual horde of gnomes, not so bad... of
course, it turns nasty pretty soon after that again. Next level up I
suspect there was a poly trap, I never found it, but... I ran away
from a nasty dragon and a mind-flayer *shudder* The mind-flayer died
in a flurry of daggers..... the dragon.... I ran.

One level up I fend off a nasty ghoul along with a giant horde of
elves and killer bees... what's this? It feels familiar here... and I
fend off a named Ghoul, that seems to be very strong...  Bee was an
elvish ranger who had died just before this char, so it was a little
eerie to bump into her.


----------------
The writing trails off here... I didn't finish, I got burnt out
writing the tale, but I'll do my best to finish.

Sokobon yielded the amulet, thankfully, which was nice after getting
the BoH from Bee's remains.

Nothing special happened after minetown and I decended into the
depths, I played carefully. I knew at this point,  I could make it,
after my last try was taken away from me. I played with a strict vegan
diet, limiting that so I couldn't get many resistances, relying
instead on getting crowned and many sacrifices instead.

No close calls on the quest, nothing stands out so long after for me
now. I got to discard my amulet of esp for the eye, which was a nice
bonus.

My main priority was getting dragon scale mail, ideally silver, but I
managed to wrangle down a black dragon at the castle, and properly get
it enchanted up with plenty of blank paper and a magic marker.

A couple of bones files in the demon levels of gehommen, but nothing
nasty or deadly. I had a careful trip, heading back up whenever my
life threatened, I made it quickly to the bottom to do the final great
rush with the amulet... only to find my silver dragon scales on the
way up, I had to keep them even with rodney chasing me. :)

The elemental planes are hazy, I made it, and used the swarms of
insects to keep myself safe from the touch of the riders. It took
three tries to find my altar, go figure.

This was my last ascencion for awhile, when I make another, I'll make
sure to write the full story in detail as I did for my previous ones.


